winit 0.30.10..0.30.13 on powerpc-apple-darwin: `platform_impl/macos/app.rs` swizzles `-[NSApplication
sendEvent:]` (method_setImplementation) and calls the saved original IMP as a plain `extern "C" fn`.
On Darwin PowerPC an Objective-C method built by Apple's GCC takes its PIC base from r12
(`mflr r0; stmw ..; mr r31,r12; addis r2,r31,..; lwz r2,..(r2); .. lwz r0,0(r2)`): the ABI puts the
callee's address in r12 for indirect calls, objc_msgSend and the dyld stubs do, but FSF GCC's Darwin
backend (rs6000_call_darwin_1: force_reg + mtctr) does not, so the call arrives with r12 = the IMP of the
last objc_msgSend (`-[NSEvent type]`) and AppKit faults at sendEvent: + 44 (alacritty 0.17.0 on 10.6.8:
EXC_BAD_ACCESS at 0 on the very first event, which is winit's own exit dummy event). On powerpc the
original implementation is added to the class as `winitOriginalSendEvent:` and reached through
objc_msgSend. 0.30.0..0.30.9 subclassed NSApplication and used `msg_send![super(..)]`, which is fine.

winit 0.30.10..0.30.13 on powerpc-apple-darwin (Mac OS X 10.6, the last PowerPC release): the macOS backend
sends these 10.7+ selectors on the window-creation and event paths, each an `unrecognized selector` (or, with
objc2's debug assertions, a panic `invalid message send to -[NSScreen backingScaleFactor]: method not found`,
alacritty 0.17.0 right after the GL config): `backingScaleFactor` (NSScreen/NSWindow, 10.7) -> 1.0, no HiDPI;
`convertRectToScreen:` (10.7) -> `convertBaseToScreen:` for the IME rect; `scrollingDeltaX/Y`,
`hasPreciseScrollingDeltas`, `momentumPhase`, `phase` (10.7) -> the classic `deltaX/Y` line deltas and
TouchPhase::Moved; `setWantsBestResolutionOpenGLSurface:` (10.7), `setTitlebarAppearsTransparent:` /
`setTitleVisibility:` (10.10), `setTabbingIdentifier:`/`setTabbingMode:` and the tab methods (10.12) skipped;
`setAppearance:`/`appearance`/NSAppearance (10.9): theme() = Light, set_theme no-op; `toggleFullScreen:`
(10.7): `set_fullscreen`/`fullscreen` are the window-level "simple" fullscreen; `performWindowDragWithEvent:`
(10.11): NotSupported. Everything else the backend sends exists in the 10.6 SDK (checked against the AppKit,
Foundation and OpenGL headers). Delegate callbacks 10.6 never invokes (occlusion, pressure, smart magnify,
fullscreen transitions) are left alone. Gated on target_arch powerpc/powerpc64: whole-item cfg copies for fns,
`#[cfg] let` for the scroll/gesture values, `util::LEGACY_MACOS` for the creation-time attributes.

